      "why": "The stage was in the output and its modulation was at nothing: a byte the page prints as that stage's depth or sensitivity stood at nought while the pair was compared. What this parameter describes is how that modulation runs, and a modulation at no depth runs the same however it is described -- a rate scales nothing, a waveform shapes nothing. So the two sets of takes are two takes of one sound. Read as a null it would say the parameter does nothing; what it says is that there was nothing for it to do. The byte that decides how much of the stage reaches the output is not read this way, because a stage at no depth is still a stage -- a chorus at none of it is a fixed delay, and mixing that in is audible."
